T1  - A STUDY OF CONTAINER HANDLING CHALLENGES AND ADOPTION OF IMPROVED REHANDLING STRATEGIES FOR THE CONTAINER RETRIEVAL PROCESS DURING THE PANDEMIC PERIOD
A1  - Subha N.
A1  - Vikkraman P.
A1  - Deepak R.
Y1  - 2021//
N2  - The breakdown of trade barriers among countries led to an enormous increase in the volume of international trade. Consequently, the amount of bulk cargo carried in containers and transported overseas exploded because of flexibility and reliability of this type of transportation. There are different types of containers that are used to carry cargo of different dimensions. Organizations normally do their cargo shipments through agents who are specialised in the logistics sector; they provide not just import, export services but also packing and warehousing. A Non-Vessel Operating Common Carriers (NVOCC) can be considered as one of these agents; a NVOCC does not have its own vessel but has its own container boxes. NVOCCs sell container space on-board mainline transport vessels, to their customers. This helps customers to avoid complications involved in export or import procedures. The study is done with the help of secondary data obtained from a Non-Vessel Operating Common Carrier (Capeline shipping llc) is analysed to understand the total number of containers that is utilized in the past. The analysis also looks into the recent pandemic situation and how it has affected the organization. Further forecasting is done about the number of containers that might be required for the upcoming year. The prediction is done using two methods: Exponential smoothing and ARIMA model are used to predict the number of containers that might be required for the upcoming year. The inventory control techniques used by the organization to release containers to customers is also understood. The container handling and rehandling methods that are utilized by the organization seems to provide a major challenge. This is mainly due to the lack of land for storage in the yard available. For solving this problem, a more feasible stacking technique is suggested which utilizes parameters such as row, tier and stack to help pick out the containers in a shuffled manner so that the reusing of the same container repeatedly can be avoided. This improved strategy that has been suggested will help improve the organization inventory management. The methods that are used to release empty containers to customers from the container yard is also analysed in the study.Copyright © 2021 EManuscript Technologies. All rights reserved.
