T1  - Dependence of parameters of impairment of consciousness on characteristics of a stroke and on epidemiological parameters of patients
T3  - 27th European Stroke Conference, ESC 2018. Athens Greece.
A1  - Kovyazina M.
A1  - Fontina K.
A1  - Moskvin V.
Y1  - 2018//
N2  - INTRODUCTION By the number of people who have suffered a stroke, Russia takes first places in the world. Disorders of cerebral circulation remain the leaders among diseases leading to adverse disabling outcomes. With the development of stroke, the risk of impairment of consciousness is very high, and the fact of impairment can be an important predictor of the severity of the course and outcome of a stroke. METHOD The study was retrospective and based on 112 medical histories of patients with stroke (54 with impairment: 37 women and 17 men aged 48 to 96 years, 58 without impairment: 29 women and 29 men aged 40 to 95 years). RESULTS D In women, impairment of consciousness occurs more often (x2 = 3.963; p <.05); D The probability of impairment of consciousness increases after 60 years ( x2= 12, 52; p <.01;); D A direct correlation between the onset of impairment and death exists ( x2= 59, 3; p <.001 ;); 0 With hemorrhagic stroke in stem structures, the depth of impairment of consciousness is maximal in comparison with other combinations of type parameters and localization of stroke (F = 7, 33; p <.01;); D The National Institutes of Health Stroke Scale score is higher with a hemorrhagic stroke type (F = 11, 8; p <.001;). DISCUSSION Usually, studies are conducted to identify the links of individual stroke parameters with the outcome of the disease and rehabilitation prognosis. Practically there are no scientific works analyzing the dependence of impairment of consciousness parameters (duration, depth) on the combination of stroke characteristics (type, localization, severity). There are no quantitative indicators of impairment of consciousness, after which irreversible consequences for the psyche and life of the patient occur. CONCLUSION The obtained data makes it possible to predict the risk groups that require the greatest attention of the rehabilitation team.
